  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2510.05611v2</id>
    <title>MADIAVE: Multi-Agent Debate for Implicit Attribute Value Extraction</title>
    <updated>2026-01-15T19:56:07Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.05611v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.05611v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Implicit Attribute Value Extraction (AVE) is essential for accurately representing products in e-commerce, as it infers latent attributes from multimodal data. Despite advances in multimodal large language models (MLLMs), implicit AVE remains challenging due to the complexity of multidimensional data and gaps in vision-text understanding. In this work, we introduce MADIAVE, a multi-agent debate framework that employs multiple MLLM agents to iteratively refine inferences. Through a series of debate rounds, agents verify and update each other's responses, thereby improving inference performance and robustness. Experiments on the ImplicitAVE dataset demonstrate that even a few rounds of debate significantly boost accuracy, especially for attributes with initially low performance. We systematically evaluate various debate configurations, including identical or different MLLM agents, and analyze how debate rounds affect convergence dynamics. Our findings highlight the potential of multi-agent debate strategies to address the limitations of single-agent approaches and offer a scalable solution for implicit AVE in multimodal e-commerce.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2025-10-07T06:27:42Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>Accepted by EACL 2026 (Findings)</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CL"/>
    <author>
      <name>Wei-Chieh Huang</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Cornelia Caragea</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
